{
  "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/gynaecological-care",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "gynaecological care"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "Preventive, diagnostic, therapeutic, and counselling services related to the gynaecological and reproductive health of women and girls, provided with respect for autonomy, privacy, informed consent, and the right to information."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "For women and girls with disabilities, accessibility also includes the physical, communication, and informational adaptation of services to individual needs, free from stereotyping and discrimination. Research indicates that infrastructural, organizational, and communication barriers, as well as interactions with healthcare professionals, may limit the quality of and effective access to care. Gynaecological care can be analysed through access to prevention, consultations, diagnostics and treatment, accessibility of facilities and equipment, communication with healthcare staff, respect for consent and privacy, and experiences of barriers and discrimination."
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "11.4"
  ],
  "broader": {
